  "frozen_findings": [
    "E7 is the most frequent coded sign in tablet c and also has the broadest local adjacency neighborhood in the training graph.",
    "G13→B11→A10 is a five-occurrence trigram; G13→B11→A10→G17→E22 occurs three times.",
    "A 12-sign sequence E1-G8-D1-B9-B3-D3-A3-G13-B11-A10-G17-E22 occurs twice.",
    "E23→B8→E10 occurs three times.",
    "The final line contains a sevenfold E19 run after G17; this is recorded as repetition only, not interpreted numerically.",
    "E22 is strongly line-final in tablet c (five line endings), making boundary behavior a testable structural property.",
    "Variant-coded signs remain separate until complementary-distribution/allograph tests are run."
  ],
  "next_tests": [
    "Freeze allograph candidate clusters using chart medium metadata without phonetic values.",
    "Score validation tablet d only after the tablet-c graph metrics and variant rules are frozen.",
    "Keep spatula i blind until the model predicts sequence/boundary properties.",
    "Compare line-final E22 and repeated formula behavior on validation/holdout witnesses.",
    "Build first-order and second-order Markov baselines and shuffled-line nulls.",
    "Test whether high-degree signs behave more like grammatical/syllabic hubs than rare name/logogram-like signs, without assigning readings."
